# Mailkin

> {{ t.oneLiner }} It is a Mail extension (MailKit) that uses Apple's on-device Translation framework: email content never leaves the Mac, and there is no account. The first {{ site.freeEmails }} translated emails are free; then a one-time purchase of €{{ site.price.eur }} / US${{ site.price.usd }} (no subscription). Requires macOS {{ site.minMacOS }} or later. Current version: {{ site.version }}.

Key facts:
- Translates incoming emails automatically when they are opened in Apple Mail, in place, keeping layout, links and images. A banner shows the source language; "Show Original" restores the original.
- Apple Mail itself has no automatic translation; macOS only offers the Translate command on selected text.
- {{ site.languageCount }} languages: {% for c in site.languages %}{{ c | langName("en") }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}.
- Works with every account added to Apple Mail (iCloud, Gmail, Outlook/Exchange, Yahoo, IMAP). Mac only; not on iPhone or iPad.
- Per-sender and per-email rules (always / never translate); per-language choice: automatic, only on request, or never.
- Does not yet translate emails you write or reply to.
- Available as a direct download from mailkin.app (license key, sold via Paddle); Mac App Store version coming soon.
- Website and app available in: {% for l in site.locales %}{{ l.name }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}.

